From 21cf8b67a9a78b835399cfc56261a8e69031262b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nekreshen@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:55:05 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] metal: resolves into any loaded tiled texture, not only
 mip levels

FIFA 19 resolves into the corner of a 2048x2048 k_4_4_4_4 texture, and into
targets whose fetched size is not a multiple of 8 (320x180 fetched, 320x184
resolved). Neither matched a resolve exactly, so each resolve dropped the
texture and the next fetch untiled it from memory again: about 10 texture
loads a frame in a match, 8 MB for the large one. Every loaded tiled 2D level
is now a target (several textures per address), and a resolve with the same
pitch and format whose rectangle starts inside the level is blitted into it at
its offset. metal_resolve_into_mips becomes metal_resolve_into_textures;
metal_resolve_into_textures_log says why a resolve was not taken.
---
 src/graphics/metal/metal_draw.h  |  27 ++++---
 src/graphics/metal/metal_draw.mm | 131 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/metal/metal_draw.h b/src/graphics/metal/metal_draw.h
